    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-7487",
      "problem": "In ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/3b91e08e311c16729f96f544c5588f86312b2420d7b416e10686f917ff6c344b.svg) we have ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/1d1b1943bb01e9de758c6010b51d0f7fd1f1f2a49ea8f47339b0ff7cf30ad0cc.svg) ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/aad9d166ef3cd66a75d8b4506ad8daa9905194fbdc286b4a67a49989d0a3708b.svg) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/75c950ee3e628eb3c3569f28f76afda4782d6a0c101da9e8768b6eb62eece0d7.svg) Which of the following statements *could* be true?\n\nI. ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/80d04a39273f746050caf7adee9d2d880c6244791a9eadc8aea6f36774c9e509.svg) is acute\n\nII. ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/3673b59a1b94b20040c5429645cf35d59dc5afd913dc40cc10bde6de6a78a982.svg) rounded to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/f5f3224583db57b9cfe323c8489ef5e5271000002b5ea253eb98fd067a858b2d.svg) decimal places\n\nIII. ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/61b4c7f5c4215d33904076ae8a44759225fd7228b43b2eb10604c7d181c49dc9.svg) rounded to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/f5f3224583db57b9cfe323c8489ef5e5271000002b5ea253eb98fd067a858b2d.svg) decimal places",
      "worked_solution": "The following triangle illustrates the information given.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/6394766fc2d6dda3833641cfb4994f835af02840ba5e8a654d21d7e3dfdba08b.png)\n\nThe law of sines states that\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/d078c57025c788d41c08927fadf724048d453125fe7b1eb47e8eafa941ab91c0.svg)\n\nIn this case, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/3965f6fff0c080b7dfff3ff2d23d652a9a4478141055e48a53a29b00f67d4896.svg)\nand therefore\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/f87f8699dce13a1827c38c0a5ad87b80358e65616d4e42ca2f600cf005b1b197.svg)\n\nThis gives\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/051bf1ed107f2432678d92d8f14a9f8402e8917ecf500bff8a97e572b96ce27b.svg)\nrounded to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/f5f3224583db57b9cfe323c8489ef5e5271000002b5ea253eb98fd067a858b2d.svg) decimal places.\n\nIn this case, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/25d1700aa8d542a4900380c801dadf7b61aa85cb1b4f4af92d2efc7aaed3ec78.svg)\n\nHowever, another solution to ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/8b963e16d2d321b429bde22460770898a1bbf18e138ec6c7cd0c21f6c728e8e2.svg) is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/b95d7304f95df77c35d514baa66c17f14a1e9239118ec3274d3b3271910205e4.svg)\n\nIn this case, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/72f0d072293e59acc5b2cf9f1234710ce7aa888e5678f29e53e2d8a7cb54e756.svg)\n\nSo, there are two possible triangles, with the following angle measures:\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/f1101a66fa07e354a30a6a54b22091da6b770bed9b62ca37e9c1c4228588ac4b.svg) ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/1d1b1943bb01e9de758c6010b51d0f7fd1f1f2a49ea8f47339b0ff7cf30ad0cc.svg) ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/61b4c7f5c4215d33904076ae8a44759225fd7228b43b2eb10604c7d181c49dc9.svg)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/883daa1a5a3cdcb402b556c34a6804e2874fb6d10567456b8c6fb3ef10948800.png)\n\n- ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/b6aa10b408f2bff96786566dd2a2b96660ebf672436c8fb5ce4b2286e09d8e8c.svg) ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/1d1b1943bb01e9de758c6010b51d0f7fd1f1f2a49ea8f47339b0ff7cf30ad0cc.svg) ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/f198a9c23a3e99c1dc13d3708c9266c3db6c2b5bddd8b6b14dd3774fcd5199b0.svg)\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14266767/assets/dea1701c56920eb219fe4ab802a0d33d94317533111ace7a9fc3fe61c49a6691.png)\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
